SLUG: services.html
TITLE: Moving Services in Kanpur — home, office, packing & storage
DESC: Home shifting, office relocation, local and intercity moving, car transport, packing, loading and storage in Kanpur. What each service includes and what drives its cost.
HEADING: Services built around how people actually move
LEAD: Every move is scoped to the job rather than sold as a package. Below is what each service actually covers, and the things that change what it costs — so you can tell in advance which parts you need.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid-3 reveal-group" data-services-grid>
        <noscript>
          <ul>
            <li>Home shifting</li>
            <li>Office and commercial relocation</li>
            <li>Local shifting</li>
            <li>Intercity and long-distance moving</li>
            <li>Car and bike transportation</li>
            <li>Packing and unpacking</li>
            <li>Loading and unloading</li>
            <li>Storage and warehousing</li>
          </ul>
        </noscript>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk" id="detail">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">In detail</span>
        <h2>What each service covers</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Most quotes are a combination of two or three of these rather than
          one. You are not obliged to take the whole list.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2">

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-home"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Home shifting</h3>
          <p>
            A full household move, run room by room. We inventory what is
            going, pack it, dismantle the furniture that needs it, load, move,
            and rebuild at the other end against the same list.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Room-by-room inventory that becomes your quote</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Beds, wardrobes and modular units dismantled and reassembled</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Cartons labelled by room so unpacking is not a treasure hunt</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What changes the price:</strong> the number of rooms, how
            much of the packing you want us to do, and the access at both ends.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/home-shifting.html">
            Home shifting in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-building"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Office &amp; commercial relocation</h3>
          <p>
            Planned around your downtime rather than ours. Workstations,
            server racks, records and furniture are moved in a sequence agreed
            in advance so the business can open on schedule.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Weekend and overnight slots, so staff return to a working office</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Desks numbered and mapped to the new floor plan before the move</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Documents moved in sealed, numbered crates</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What changes the price:</strong> headcount, how much IT has
            to be disconnected and reconnected, and lift access in both buildings.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/office-relocation.html">
            Office relocation in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pin"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Local shifting</h3>
          <p>
            A move within the same city, usually finished inside a single day.
            The vehicle is sized to your inventory so you are not paying for
            empty space, and the crew stays with the job from start to finish.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Same-day completion for most flats up to 3 BHK</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Early starts to work around society timing restrictions</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>One crew end to end, not a handover halfway</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What changes the price:</strong> floor and lift access,
            how far the truck can park from the door, and the volume.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/local-shifting.html">
            Local shifting in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-route"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Intercity &amp; long-distance moving</h3>
          <p>
            City-to-city relocation in a dedicated vehicle. Your consignment
            is not consolidated with other households unless you choose a
            shared load to bring the cost down.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Dedicated vehicle by default; shared part-load offered if you want it</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Driver's contact shared with you at dispatch</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Delivery window agreed before the vehicle leaves</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What changes the price:</strong> distance, the size of the
            vehicle your inventory needs, and whether you share the load.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/intercity-relocation.html">
            Intercity moving in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Car &amp; bike transportation</h3>
          <p>
            Vehicles travel in a covered carrier rather than being driven
            across, so nothing is added to the odometer and the paint is not
            exposed to the road for a thousand kilometres.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Covered carrier, loaded and strapped at the wheels</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Condition noted and photographed at both ends</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Can run on the same booking as your household goods</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What you need:</strong> the registration papers, and the
            tank at roughly a quarter full.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/vehicle-transport.html">
            Vehicle transport in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-box"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Packing &amp; unpacking</h3>
          <p>
            The part of a move that decides whether anything breaks. Fragile
            items are wrapped in layers and boxed by room, and every carton is
            labelled with its room and contents before it leaves the floor.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Bubble wrap, corrugated sheets and stretch film as the item needs</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Furniture hardware bagged and taped to the item it came off</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Unpacking and packing waste removed if you want it</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> having us pack only the kitchen, glass and
            electronics — and doing clothes and books yourself — is the
            single easiest way to bring a quote down.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/packing-unpacking.html">
            Packing in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-lift"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Loading &amp; unloading</h3>
          <p>
            Labour only, for when you have your own vehicle or have packed
            yourself. Heavy items go in first and low, fragile cartons ride on
            top, and the load is strapped so nothing shifts in transit.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Trolleys and lifting straps for heavy furniture</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Stairs and buildings without a lift planned for, not improvised</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Loading sheet signed off with you before the vehicle moves</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>What changes the price:</strong> the floor, the lift, and
            the carry distance from door to vehicle.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/loading-unloading.html">
            Loading and unloading in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-warehouse"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Storage &amp; warehousing</h3>
          <p>
            For when possession dates do not line up. Goods are inventoried
            in, wrapped and held off the floor, then delivered out when you are
            ready — charged by duration and separately from the move.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Short and long-term, from a few days upwards</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Inventoried in and out, so you know exactly what is held</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Rate confirmed in writing before anything goes in</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>Worth knowing:</strong> tell us as early as you can if your
            new home may not be ready. Arranging storage in advance costs less
            than arranging it on the day.
          </p>
          <a class="link-cta" href="/services/storage-warehousing.html">
            Storage in detail
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Photographs of real jobs. Generated by
       tools/gallery/add-photo-strips.ps1 -- edit the mapping there, not
       here, or the next run will not know this strip exists. -->
  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk" aria-labelledby="shots-services" data-photo-strip>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">From our own jobs</span>
        <h2 id="shots-services">What the work looks like</h2>
        <p class="lead">Whichever service you need, the packing standard is the same one. These are from household and office jobs in Kanpur.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workshots">
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/crew-wrapping-furniture-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/crew-wrapping-furniture-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/crew-wrapping-furniture-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="A crew member drawing stretch film around a large piece of furniture indoors."
               width="301" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <figcaption class="workshot__cap">Stretch film goes on by hand, layer by layer</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/trunks-with-edge-protection-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/trunks-with-edge-protection-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/trunks-with-edge-protection-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="Trunks and boxes wrapped and finished with studded edge protection, stacked indoors."
               width="301" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </figure>
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/packed-goods-stacked-indoors-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/packed-goods-stacked-indoors-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/packed-goods-stacked-indoors-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="Cartons, wrapped furniture and a storage crate stacked together indoors."
               width="301" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6"><a class="link-cta" href="/gallery.html">
        All 44 photographs
        <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
      </a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Not sure which of these you need?</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Describe the move and we will tell you which parts are worth paying
          for and which you can do yourself.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Request a callback</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/contact.html">Contact us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
